# Lecture 12C

## Set #7: Bioethics in Biotechnology
## Dr. Neil Voss
## Nov 19, 2026

=== layout: bookend

# Learning Objectives

@body

- Use a result from a study to explain what a biotechnology can do.
- Decide what else you would need to know before you would use it.
- Explain who gets to make that decision and who has to live with it.

@citation

[UNESCO, Universal Declaration on Bioethics and Human Rights](https://www.unesco.org/en/legal-affairs/universal-declaration-bioethics-and-human-rights)

=== layout: definitions

# Terms for the Discussion

@body

- *Consent:* a voluntary decision based on understandable information.
- *Oversight:* independent review of what a project does and how it manages risk.
- *Evidence:* observations that support or weaken a specific claim.

@citation

[The Belmont Report (1979)](https://www.hhs.gov/ohrp/regulations-and-policy/belmont-report/read-the-belmont-report/index.html)

